  "$doc": "The flow manifest (backlog item 22). Every interactive element on a board of a wired page carries data-flow=\"n\" (1..n per board, badges drawn by the shell); each number has exactly one edge here, whose `to` lists every outcome: a board, a declared terminal, or an explicit gap (a design still owed — honest, greppable, reported by check-flows.mjs and drawn on the generated maps). Repeated per-post elements are tagged on the first post instance only. `entries` declares how a screen is reached other than by a tap (app open, mail link, time); a screen on a wired page must be an entry or an edge target.",
  "wired": ["entry", "money", "feed"],
  "terminals": {
    "back": "Back — returns to the previous screen",
    "self": "Acts on this screen — state changes in place",
    "os": "Hands off to the OS — browser download, mail app, system sheet"
  },
  "scanExempt": {
    "VouchBackPad": "the scrim wash covers the shell — its semantic elements (band, nav, the vouch card's own controls) are inactive in this state; only the parked pad is live",
